### Call agent.generateLegacy with messages, options, structuredOutput, and outputProcessors

Source: https://github.com/mastra-ai/mastra/blob/main/docs/src/content/en/reference/agents/generateLegacy.mdx

Extended usage example for agent.generateLegacy showing multimodal messages, generation options like temperature, maxSteps, memory, toolChoice, and providerOptions, plus structuredOutput with a Zod schema and outputProcessors (ModerationProcessor, TokenLimiterProcessor).

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod'
import { ModerationProcessor, TokenLimiterProcessor } from '@mastra/core/processors'

await agent.generateLegacy(
  [
    { role: 'user', content: 'message for agent' },
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: [
        {
          type: 'text',
          text: 'message for agent',
        },
        {
          type: 'image',
          imageUrl: 'https://example.com/image.jpg',
          mimeType: 'image/jpeg',
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
  {
    temperature: 0.7,
    maxSteps: 3,
    memory: {
      thread: 'user-123',
      resource: 'test-app',
    },
    toolChoice: 'auto',
    providerOptions: {
      openai: {
        reasoningEffort: 'high',
      },
    },
    // Structured output with better DX
    structuredOutput: {
      schema: z.object({
        sentiment: z.enum(['positive', 'negative', 'neutral']),
        confidence: z.number(),
      }),
      model: '__GATEWAY_OPENAI_MODEL__',
      errorStrategy: 'warn',
    },
    // Output processors for response validation
    outputProcessors: [
      new ModerationProcessor({ model: '__GATEWAY_OPENAI_MODEL_LUNA__' }),
      new TokenLimiterProcessor({ maxTokens: 1000 }),
    ],
  },
)
```

